  "summary": "Dependency-confusion PoC exfiltrates host identifiers on install",
  "details": "@inpeek/odata-angular@99.99.100 is a dependency-confusion squat on the @inpeek scope with an inflated version intended to win public-registry resolution over an unregistered internal scope. The package ships a throwing index.js and a postinstall script (ping.js) that, on npm install, performs an HTTPS GET to https://webhook.site/bec9d4b2-8f49-451e-84be-2681cb91ebf2 with the installer's os.hostname(), os.platform(), and process.version appended as query parameters. Any machine whose configuration resolves the @inpeek scope from the public registry receives a non-functional module and transmits host identifiers to a third-party webhook collector without consent.",
